  "prompt": "Could you write a captivating short story beginning with the sentence: The old abandoned house at the end of the street held a secret that no one had ever discovered.",
  "answer": "The old abandoned house at the end of the street held a secret that no one had ever discovered.\n\nAt least, that’s what everyone said.\n\nMara had heard it from the butcher, the bus driver, and the children who dared one another to touch the rusted gate. She heard it again the night the house began blinking.\n\nOne window lit up. Then another. Not with the warm yellow of a lamp, but with a cold blue glow that pulsed like a heartbeat.\n\nMara crossed the street.\n\nThe gate sighed open beneath her hand. Inside, dust lay thick over the floorboards, except for a narrow trail of fresh footprints leading upstairs. They were small, bare, and wet.\n\nAt the top of the stairs stood a little girl in a red coat.\n\nMara stopped. “Are you lost?”\n\nThe girl shook her head. “You’re late.”\n\n“Late for what?”\n\nThe girl pointed to a door at the end of the hall. Behind it came a sound Mara knew from childhood: her mother’s laugh.\n\nBut her mother had been gone for twelve years.\n\nMara reached for the handle. The little girl vanished.\n\nOn the other side of the door, someone whispered her name.\n\nAnd from the street below, every house on the block went dark.",
